{"id":89,"flavor":[{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration of its nose, it lost its sense of smell."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Because they scatter germs everywhere, they’ve long been targeted for extermination, leading to a steep decline in their population."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Their food sources have decreased, and their numbers have declined sharply. Sludge ponds are being built to prevent their extinction."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"After recent environmental improvements, this Pokémon is now hardly seen at all. People speculate that it may go extinct at some point."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"The stench it gives off will make your nose scrunch up. Still, there are Muk fans who think that’s a good thing."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"This Pokémon’s favorite food is anything that is repugnantly filthy. In dirty towns where people think nothing of throwing away litter on the streets, Muk are certain to gather."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"From Muk’s body seeps a foul fluid that gives off a nose-bendingly horrible stench. Just one drop of this Pokémon’s body fluid can turn a pool stagnant and rancid."},{"games":["Y","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact."},{"games":["X","HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"They love to gather in smelly areas where sludge accumulates, making the stench around them worse."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"It’s so stinky! Muk’s body contains toxic elements, and any plant will wilt when it passes by."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"Its body is made of a powerful poison. Touching it accidentally will cause a fever that requires bed rest."},{"games":["LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"Thickly covered with a filthy, vile sludge. It is so toxic, even its footprints contain poison."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"It is usually undetectable because it blends in with the ground. Touching it can cause terrible poisoning."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It prefers warm and humid habitats. In the summertime, the toxic substances in its body intensify, making MUK reek like putrid kitchen garbage."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"As it moves, a very strong poison leaks from it, making the ground there barren for three years."},{"games":["Yellow"],"text":"Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration, it lost its sense of smell."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Stench","hidden":false,"description":"By releasing a stench when attacking, the Pokémon may cause the target to flinch."},{"name":"Sticky Hold","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon's held items cling to its sticky body and cannot be removed by other Pokémon."},{"name":"Poison Touch","hidden":true,"description":"May poison a target when the Pokémon makes contact."}],"eggGroups":["Amorphous"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"urban","color":"Purple","shape":"Arms","evolution":{"id":88,"name":"Grimer","condition":null,"children":[{"id":89,"name":"Muk","condition":"Lv. 38","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,1],[1,106],[1,139],[1,189],[12,50],[15,124],[18,341],[21,107],[26,92],[29,188],[32,482],[37,103],[40,441],[46,151],[52,562],[57,262]],"machine":[491,34,280,109,174,399,91,409,203,263,126,7,53,374,411,264,202,416,441,114,270,506,63,8,286,282,808,679,118,341,189,220,398,182,240,156,157,317,201,184,247,214,188,482,180,164,241,129,36,269,851,168,87,9,85,92,390,474,428],"egg":[],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv10-124","name":"Team Rocket's Muk","set":"Destined Rivals","date":"2025-05-30","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"124","artist":null,"img":"sv10/124"},{"id":"sv3pt5-89","name":"Muk","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"89","artist":"Nisota Niso","img":"sv3pt5/89"},{"id":"sv1-127","name":"Muk","set":"Scarlet &